Article 4 The application shall specify the following matters:
(1) The name, gender, age, work unit and address of the applicant;
(2) The country of the court that rendered the judgment, the result and date of the judgment;
(3) The circumstances of being summoned and responding to the lawsuit;
(4) The reasons for the application and the request;
(5) Other matters that need to be explained.

Article 12 Upon examination, if a foreign court's divorce judgment falls under any of the following circumstances, it shall not be recognized:
(1) The judgment has not yet taken legal effect;
(2) The foreign court that rendered the judgment does not have jurisdiction over the case;
(3) The judgment was made in the absence of the defendant without lawful summons;
(4) The divorce case between the parties is being tried or has already been adjudicated by a Chinese court, or a judgment on the divorce case between the parties rendered by a court of a third country has been recognized by a Chinese court;
(5) The judgment violates the basic principles of Chinese law or endangers the national sovereignty, security and social public interest of China.
